From: mscharged-port
Subject: Switch the desktop picture while the game runs
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: host presentation, no game behaviour change.

The menus' DISPLAY page switches the picture style (smooth, sharp or the
TV's signal) and the TV border while the game runs, as it already switches
stretching: the next presented frame uses them, and the display copy's
flicker filter follows the picture as at configuration.

diff --git a/include/aurora/video.h b/include/aurora/video.h
index cb06385..c3bff7a 100644
--- a/include/aurora/video.h
+++ b/include/aurora/video.h
@@ -98,6 +98,10 @@ void aurora_configure_video_output_hardware(const AuroraVIOutputConfig* config);
 // (stretch) or keep its 16:9 or 4:3 shape, from the next presented frame. A
 // window-sized EFB (VILockAspectRatio) follows the picture's new shape.
 void aurora_set_video_output_stretch(bool stretch);
+// Owner thread, after configuration: the desktop picture (AuroraDesktopPicture)
+// and the TV frame (SIGNAL only) from the next presented frame, as configured
+// above; the display copy's flicker filter follows the picture.
+void aurora_set_video_output_picture(uint8_t desktop_picture, bool tv_frame);
 // Owner thread, after configuration: from the next presented frame the window
 // shows the picture blurred (behind a host panel), or sharp again. Host
 // presentation only: screenshots and the game's own frames stay sharp.
diff --git a/lib/gfx/scanout.cpp b/lib/gfx/scanout.cpp
index f667edf..502156f 100644
--- a/lib/gfx/scanout.cpp
+++ b/lib/gfx/scanout.cpp
@@ -1004,6 +1004,19 @@ void aurora_set_video_output_stretch(bool stretch) {
   // The window-sized EFB follows the presented picture's new shape.
   aurora::window::set_frame_buffer_fill(stretch);
 }
+void aurora_set_video_output_picture(uint8_t desktop_picture, bool tv_frame) {
+  if (desktop_picture > AURORA_DESKTOP_SHARP) throw std::invalid_argument("Unknown native desktop picture");
+  auto& state = aurora::gfx::scanout::State();
+  {
+    std::lock_guard lock(state.mutex);
+    if (!state.configured) return;
+    aurora::gfx::scanout::RequireOwner(state);
+    state.desktop_picture = desktop_picture;
+    state.tv_frame = tv_frame && desktop_picture == AURORA_DESKTOP_SIGNAL;
+  }
+  // Smooth and sharp desktop pictures skip the display copy's flicker filter.
+  aurora::gfx::xfb::set_flicker_filter(desktop_picture == AURORA_DESKTOP_SIGNAL);
+}
